WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.950
Touch a snail gently
between its tentacles,

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.640
and it pulls them in.

3
00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:07.030
Touch it again, and again.

4
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:11.030
Each time it pulls them in
less, and comes out sooner.

5
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:16.320
In one set of illustrative data, the
time to re-emerge fell from 48 seconds to

6
00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:17.520
9.

7
00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:22.310
You do it too: after a while, you
stop noticing a ticking clock.

8
00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:24.980
So why does an animal's
reaction to a harmless,

9
00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:27.580
repeated touch fade away?

10
00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.380
In this mission, you'll plan a fair test:

11
00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:34.320
same touch, same place, snail after snail.

12
00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:38.430
Then you'll read the data and
test each possible explanation.

13
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:43.340
Your mission: explain why an animal stops
reacting to a harmless touch that keeps

14
00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:44.200
coming back.
